m</surname><given-names>NP</given-names></name><name><surname>Bartholomeu</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name><name><surname>Gobatto</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Kokubun</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Brum</surname><given-names>PC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Maximal lactate steady state in running mice: effect of exercise training</article-title><source>Clin Exp Pharmacol Physiol</source><year>2007</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>760</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17600553</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1440-1681.2007.04635.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gobatto</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Mello</surname><given-names>MAR</given-names></name><name><surname>Sibuya</surname><given-names>CY</given-names></name><name><surname>Azevedo</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Santos</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Kokubun</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Maximal lactate stedy state in rats submitted to swimming exercise</article-title><source>Comparative Biochemistry and Physiology</source><year>2001</year><volume>130</volume><fpage>21</fpage><lpage>27</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11672680</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S1095-6433(01)00362-2</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Beneke</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Methodological aspects of maximal lactate steady state-implications for performance testing</article-title><source>Eur J Appl Physiol</source><year>2003</year><volume>89</volume><fpage>95</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12627312</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi